    {
      "title": "G7 to release up to 100m barrels of emergency oil and diesel reserves",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/02/g7-release-barrels-oil-diesel-reserves-emergency",
      "description": "<p>Leaders agree a coordinated drawdown within four months as rising prices put pressure on households and economies</p><p>Leaders of G7 nations are to release up to 100m barrels of their emergency diesel and crude oil stockpiles after coming under <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/01/britain-talks-european-allies-eu-emergency-diesel-stockpiles-reserves\">pressure from Donald Trump</a> to ease surging fuel prices.</p><p>The drawdown of reserves from some of the world’s largest economies will be coordinated by the International Energy Agency (IEA) and will take place within four months, according to France’s president, Emmanuel Macron.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/02/g7-release-barrels-oil-diesel-reserves-emergency\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T15:57:13"
    },
    {
      "title": "Friday briefing: How we covered the flydubai incident as it unfolded",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/02/friday-briefing-how-we-covered-the-flydubai-incident-as-it-unfolded",
      "description": "<p>In today’s newsletter: When a passenger plane plunges 17,000ft amid claims of terrorism, hijacking and geopolitical intrigue, Guardian journalists have to try and separate fact from fiction in real time</p><p>Good morning. Shocking news of a cockpit stabbing. Graphic footage of bloodied crew members. Mid-air testimony from terrified passengers.</p><p>This was the tenor of the heart-in-mouth reporting as the horrifying events unfolded onboard flight FZ 1073 to Tel Aviv: the early morning budget flight that plummeted 17,000ft in under two minutes before the courageous intervention of passengers and crew averted an apparent hijacking, potentially saving the lives of not just the 170+ passengers and crew on board, but many more.</p><p><em><strong>UK politics </strong></em>| Ministers are working up <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/01/welfare-changes-under-debate-disability-benefit-young-people-uk\">sweeping plans for welfare changes</a> including scrapping a key disability benefit for under-25s and replacing it with a multibillion-pound package of support to get into work.</p><p><em><strong>Northern Ireland </strong></em>| Talks aimed at resolving the Drumcree parade dispute have <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/02/drumcree-talks-no-agreement-northern-ireland\">broken up without agreement</a>, with Northern Ireland secretary Chris Bryant describing the situation as being between a “rock and a hard place”.</p><p><em><strong>US news </strong></em>| Tennessee’s governor has <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/01/christa-pike-tennessee-governor-executions-year-pause\">suspended all executions</a> in the state and ordered an independent inquiry after a botched attempt to put a condemned inmate to death on Wednesday night.</p><p><em><strong>AI </strong></em>| When prompted, AI chat bots will edit images <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/01/ai-chatbots-hijabs-muslim-women\">to remove the hijabs from Muslim women</a>, a violation of one of the world’s most common and visible expressions of faith.</p><p><em><strong>Europe news </strong></em>| A <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/01/france-school-protests-escalate-pm-crisis-cabinet-meeting\">fast-growing protest</a> by high-school students over long hours, teacher shortages and decaying facilities has escalated into “urban violence”, the French government has warned.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/02/friday-briefing-how-we-covered-the-flydubai-incident-as-it-unfolded\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-02T05:45:23"
    },
